cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you refer to this work, please cite it as below, and please cite the published
  article (doi:10.1007/s00220-022-04521-8) for the results it contains. The revised
  manuscript in this repository is not the version of record and has not been refereed.
title: >-
  Conformal field theory from lattice fermions: a critical re-reading, a revised
  manuscript, and a note on the Zini-Wang comparison
abstract: >-
  An adversarial re-examination of Osborne and Stottmeister, Conformal Field Theory
  from Lattice Fermions, Commun. Math. Phys. 398 (2023) 219-289. Eight findings are
  recorded, among them an invalid domination step that recurs in three places, an
  error estimate that is infinite as stated in the Ramond sector, three unstated
  regularity thresholds of which the largest is K >= 9, and a normalisation that read
  literally gives central charge (L/pi)^2. No theorem statement is affected. The
  repository contains a revised manuscript repairing all eight and adding sharp rates,
  Duhamel estimates, an unconditional proof of the Virasoro correlation-function
  theorem via a scale-uniform energy bound, a reconstruction theorem for smeared
  Koo-Saleur approximants and an explicit quantum-simulation error budget; a separate
  note showing that the obstruction to the Zini-Wang low-energy scaling limit is
  constancy of the GNS multiplicity rather than purity; and nineteen numpy scripts
  supporting every quoted number.
type: software
authors:
